## 7. Key Architecture Patterns to Reuse

### Pattern 1: Token-Suffixed Dynamic IDs

Append dynamic IDs to tokens for filtered views:
```
base_token_t          → all records
base_token_t_123      → records filtered by ID 123
```

Backend extracts the ID:
```php
$parts = explode('_', $token);
$lastPart = end($parts);
if (is_numeric($lastPart)) {
    $conditions[] = ['column' => 'table.id', 'operator' => '=', 'value' => $lastPart];
}
```

### Pattern 2: Conditional Token Selection in Views

Use request parameters to decide which token to render:
```blade
@if(request('product_id'))
    <div data-skeleton-table-set="central_product_companies_t_{{ request('product_id') }}"></div>
@elseif(request('li_company_id'))
    <div data-skeleton-table-set="central_sun_master_accounts_t_{{ request('li_company_id') }}"></div>
@endif
```

### Pattern 3: CSV → IN Query Pipeline

```php
$ids = DB::table('source_table')
    ->where('id', $id)
    ->pluck('csv_column')                    // Get CSV string
    ->flatMap(fn($s) => array_map('intval', explode(',', $s)))  // Split and cast
    ->filter()                               // Remove empty/zero
    ->unique()                               // Deduplicate
    ->values()
    ->toArray();

$conditions[] = ['column' => 'target.id', 'operator' => 'IN', 'value' => $ids];
```

### Pattern 4: Dual-Purpose Detail Page

Same view serves two purposes based on query parameter:
```php
if ($companyId) {
    // Company-centric view: show leads, label = "Leads"
    $data['is_product_view'] = false;
} elseif ($productId) {
    // Product-centric view: show contacts, label = "Contacts"
    $data['is_product_view'] = true;
}
```

### Pattern 5: Custom Column Transformations

Make any column interactive without changing the frontend table component:
```php
// Turn a text column into a clickable link
['type' => 'modify', 'column' => 'name',
 'view' => '<a href="/detail?id=::id::">::name::</a>', 'renderHtml' => true]

// Add an extra action button column
['type' => 'addon', 'column' => 'Actions',
 'view' => '<button data-id="::id::">Edit</button>', 'renderHtml' => true]
```

